Z||000005||Seanh||07-15-2001||05:52 PM||||We just rice on their roof around here......<P>I had some in my car the other day, so I used it. I was heading up North of town to the park, and there are some pretty sharp "S" curves thru that part of town. I noticed a Red riced civic pulling thru them pretty hard so I stomped on it (not the Fiero, driving my beater [I mean resto project] Porsche 924. I took him thru the curves and it must have been my lucky day cuz the light ahead just turned red (any other time I'd be pissed that it turned red) We were the first 2 car there, so I had to go for it. I reved my little beat to crap 924's OHC 4 banger and played with the clutch a little bit to get him to go for it. He didn't want to race, said it wasn't worth his time. Finally he started revving his weedwhacker engine too. Light turned green, I dropped at 4500 (should have droped at 3500-3800) and smoked the tires a bit, and took him off the line. He did a small front wheel drive burnout and was off after me. I shifted into 2nd at redline (6500) and pulled even further on him. He was never ahead of me. I stopped then, because it was obvious he couldn't keep up. Man that guy must have felt horrible...He got beat by an 81 Porsche 924 with no hood, broken windshield, and covered in windowchalk for decoration  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> . We saw the car later that day in a parking lot, so we sprikled rice all around it.||||reg||1
