Z||000012||Galen||07-16-2001||02:47 AM||||Simple Fiero, I direct you to that quote the old wiseman told me.. "He who believes what he is told before he fully understands talks too much"<P>the term 'ricer' is not meant as a 'racist' term. Lets see what the term 'ricer' means from the website  <A HREF="http://www.riceboypage.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.riceboypage.com</A> .... <P>"The typical Rice-Boy can be identified by his car, or rather what he does to it. Generally, Rice-Boy will start out with a car that was not meant to go fast (typically a Honda Civic), and attempt to 'fix it up,' usually consisting of aftermarket rims, lowering springs and an aftermarket exhaust system with a large exhaust tip. " ... "Rice-Boys do not exclusively drive Japanese cars. There are quite a few fake Mustang '5.0's and Camaro Z28's out there, as well as quite a few strange looking Neons. "<P>I call people ricers, does that make me racist? Then I guess I am if it does. As are alot of people. "We have two ears, one mouth. Listen carefully before you open that mouth".<P>Now, can we all just be friendly?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"It may be the opinion of the court, but its still wrong"</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/download.html" TARGET=_blank>Download FieroProject.com Chat Client v1.22 Today</A>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Mach10||07-16-2001||02:59 AM||||'S funny. Most of the truly tasteless hack jobs done to poor 4-door econo-boxes in Winnipeg are driven by white people. The well-done-up 'ricers' are probably 45:55 split between white and asian. I don't think you're an *******  'cos of the car you drive. Nope, I think you are an *******  'cos your shitty sick goat exhaust is louder than my stereo, you just made a 4-lane change without signals in front of me, and locked up your ugly-ass 19" wheels.<BR>The fact that I wouldn't be caught dead in your car has nothing to do with race or creed. Personal preference.<BR>Have a nice day, friend.<P><BR>Edit:<BR>Actually, I did some thinking, and I have found what it is exactly about the ricer phenomenon that I hate most. It's the "Looks before Go" mentality that is sweeping the custom car market. I really can't stand that. If you're gonna make your car into a high-tech, futuristic machine, then at least make it fast. I'm sorry, 0-60 in 9 seconds isn't fast. 16s 1/4s isn't fast. You show me a 'teg all done up with ugly wheels, I'll laugh. I'll stop laughing when I see it break 13-14 seconds. <p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-16-2001).]||||reg||7
